# A program has one `main`, in the file it runs from. A used module's file
# with its own `main`, or with bare top-level statements (an implicit `main`),
# is an error: both used to be dropped without a word, so what ran depended
# on which file the build started from.
using Noisy
using Chatty

main do
  IO.printLine(shout(greet("kex")))
end
